    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0149" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg101"/>

                <head>No.71.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward
                        to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 12, 1877</date>.
                        (Received June 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 240]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to hand to you herewith a
                    letter which I have received from the consul at Amoy, in regard to the
                    establishment of a municipal body, for the control of roads, &amp;c, in the
                    district occupied by foreigners at that port, and my response thereto.</p>
                <p>I shall hereafter send to you the report of the case at Shanghai, referred to in
                    my dispatch, with such remarks on the general subject as may seem pertinent.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d71-a1.xml" xpointer="d71-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d71-a2.xml" xpointer="d71-a2"/>
